From: wangjontao <54728149+wangjontao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: ignore unmapped PHY nested IRQs

On GIELINK G33Pro with MT7531, a switch PHY interrupt status bit can
be observed before a Linux IRQ mapping exists for that hwirq.
irq_find_mapping() then returns 0 and handle_nested_irq(0) dereferences
a NULL irq_desc, causing a fatal data abort at address 0xac.

Only dispatch mapped nested IRQs. The switch interrupt status was
already acknowledged before walking the PHY bits, so an unmapped or
spurious bit can safely be skipped.

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -2055,8 +2055,9 @@ mt7530_irq_thread_fn(int irq, void *dev_id)
 		if (BIT(p) & val) {
 			unsigned int irq;
 
 			irq = irq_find_mapping(priv->irq_domain, p);
-			handle_nested_irq(irq);
+			if (irq)
+				handle_nested_irq(irq);
 			handled = true;
 		}
 	}
